{
 "turns": [
  {
   "idx": 0,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Hi, I'm Maeve Gallagher. I'm a licensed clinical social worker, and today is really about getting to know you. Could you start by confirming your full name and date of birth?",
   "start": 0.08,
   "end": 10.7
  },
  {
   "idx": 1,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Rashid Al -Aman, February 17, 1974.",
   "start": 11.36,
   "end": 15.08
  },
  {
   "idx": 2,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Thanks, Rashid. And is 216 -555 -0139 still a good number for you?",
   "start": 16.02,
   "end": 22.98
  },
  {
   "idx": 3,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Yes, that's my cell.",
   "start": 23.48,
   "end": 24.42
  },
  {
   "idx": 4,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Great. So what made you decide to come in? Honestly,",
   "start": 25.28,
   "end": 28.34
  },
  {
   "idx": 5,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "my wife Samira pushed me. I got laid off 6 weeks ago. 19 years at Tri -County Logistics I ran warehouse operations and one Tuesday they just called me in and that was it.",
   "start": 28.64,
   "end": 40.16
  },
  {
   "idx": 6,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "19 years. That's a big loss. How have you been feeling since then?",
   "start": 40.76,
   "end": 44.64
  },
  {
   "idx": 7,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Down mostly, kind of useless. And I'm short with the kids which isn't me. I worry about money all the time, the mortgage, my son starting college next year.",
   "start": 45.7,
   "end": 55.02
  },
  {
   "idx": 8,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "What does a typical day look like right now?",
   "start": 55.58,
   "end": 58.34
  },
  {
   "idx": 9,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "I sleep until 10, which I never did. I send out a few applications, then I'm on the couch. I stopped going to my Saturday basketball with the guys. I just don't want to explain it.",
   "start": 58.92,
   "end": 70.1
  },
  {
   "idx": 10,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "How's your appetite?",
   "start": 70.59,
   "end": 71.19
  },
  {
   "idx": 11,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "I'm eating more honestly, junk mostly.",
   "start": 72.05,
   "end": 74.23
  },
  {
   "idx": 12,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "And before the layoff, how were you doing? Any time in your life you felt like this?",
   "start": 75.18,
   "end": 79.46
  },
  {
   "idx": 13,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No, I was fine. I've never seen a counselor or anything before this.",
   "start": 80.1,
   "end": 83.92
  },
  {
   "idx": 14,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Any panic attacks, or feeling like your heart is racing and you can't breathe.",
   "start": 83.92,
   "end": 88.72
  },
  {
   "idx": 15,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No, not that, more like a knot in my stomach. What about alcohol,",
   "start": 89.64,
   "end": 92.74
  },
  {
   "idx": 16,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "smoking, any other substances?",
   "start": 93.44,
   "end": 94.72
  },
  {
   "idx": 17,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "I don't drink, I smoked for years but I quit ten years ago when my daughter was born, nothing else.",
   "start": 95.48,
   "end": 101.04
  },
  {
   "idx": 18,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Good for you on the quitting. I'm going to ask you something I ask everyone. Have you had any thoughts of ending your life or of hurting yourself?",
   "start": 101.74,
   "end": 109.58
  },
  {
   "idx": 19,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No, no, I'd never do that to my family.",
   "start": 110.2,
   "end": 112.22
  },
  {
   "idx": 20,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Any thoughts of hurting anyone else? Maybe your old employer.",
   "start": 112.22,
   "end": 115.76
  },
  {
   "idx": 21,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Ah, no, I'm angry, but no.",
   "start": 116.26,
   "end": 117.54
  },
  {
   "idx": 22,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Thank you for being straight with me. The two questionnaires you filled out, your PHQ -9 for depression is 11, and your GED -7 for anxiety is 10. So both in the moderate range. And what I'm seeing today, your casually dressed, good eye contact, your speech is normal, your mood sounds down and a bit anxious, and your thinking is clear and logical.",
   "start": 118.08,
   "end": 139.28
  },
  {
   "idx": 23,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "That's fair.",
   "start": 139.72,
   "end": 140.26
  },
  {
   "idx": 24,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "What's been helping, even a little.",
   "start": 140.26,
   "end": 142.28
  },
  {
   "idx": 25,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Walking the dog and Samira, she's been great. She's picking up extra shifts at the hospital though so I feel guilty about that too.",
   "start": 143.48,
   "end": 150.6
  },
  {
   "idx": 26,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "So here's my impression. What you're going through sounds like an adjustment disorder with mixed anxiety and depressed mood. Basically, a strong emotional reaction to a big stressful change, the job loss. It's very common, and it usually responds well to therapy.",
   "start": 151.24,
   "end": 168.38
  },
  {
   "idx": 27,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Okay, so what do we do?",
   "start": 168.86,
   "end": 170.36
  },
  {
   "idx": 28,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "I'd like to meet weekly, about an hour each time. We'll use a CBT approach and work on behavioral activation, which means rebuilding some structure. To start, I want you up by 7, 30 on weekdays, a set two -hour block for jobs searching each morning, and one call to a basketball friend this week.",
   "start": 171.16,
   "end": 190.18
  },
  {
   "idx": 29,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "I can do that, maybe not the basketball call, but I'll try.",
   "start": 190.78,
   "end": 194.12
  },
  {
   "idx": 30,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Also, Tri -County should have offered outplacement services with your severance. It's worth calling HR to use those. And if Samira wants to join a session later on, that's welcome.",
   "start": 194.84,
   "end": 206.14
  },
  {
   "idx": 31,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "I didn't even think about outplacement.",
   "start": 206.93,
   "end": 208.87
  },
  {
   "idx": 32,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Before you leave, we'll fill out a short safety plan together. If you ever start having thoughts of hurting yourself, you can call or text 988 anytime, day or night. And if the mood gets worse despite therapy, we can talk about seeing one of our psychiatrists, but I don't think we're there.",
   "start": 209.61,
   "end": 227.55
  },
  {
   "idx": 33,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Understood.",
   "start": 228.29,
   "end": 228.67
  },
  {
   "idx": 34,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Our next session is next Thursday, October 1st, at 4 o 'clock.",
   "start": 229.43,
   "end": 233.33
  },
  {
   "idx": 35,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Thursday works thank you Maeve, this helped more than I expected.",
   "start": 233.85,
   "end": 236.95
  }
 ],
